1
00:00:00,765 --> 00:00:02,695
(Bernadette:)Don't take this the wrong way,
but how many

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,970
(Bernadette:)of these little booze balls
have you had?

3
00:00:05,935 --> 00:00:07,805
(Howard:)You don't think I'm a leader?

4
00:00:07,805 --> 00:00:10,205
(Bernadette:)I was kidding.
Of course you are.

5
00:00:10,207 --> 00:00:12,477
(Howard:)Right. I couldn't change
if I wanted to.

6
00:00:12,476 --> 00:00:15,546
(Bernadette:)You better not change,
because I love who you are.

7
00:00:15,546 --> 00:00:18,146
(Bernadette:)Now, will you need help cleaning
all this up when you're done

8
00:00:18,149 --> 00:00:20,119
(Bernadette:)or can you do it
all by yourself?

9
00:00:20,117 --> 00:00:21,617
(Howard:)All by myself.

10
00:00:21,619 --> 00:00:23,889
(Bernadette:)There's my big boss man.

11
00:00:27,357 --> 00:00:30,927
(Sheldon:)So, often on the front
of the locomotive

12
00:00:30,928 --> 00:00:33,958
(Sheldon:)is a large iron wedge

13
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:36,394
(Sheldon:)for clearing objects
off the tracks.

14
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,200
(Sheldon:)Now, while commonly
known as a cowcatcher,

15
00:00:39,203 --> 00:00:42,973
(Sheldon:)I prefer the more
accurate "cow exploder."

16
00:00:44,407 --> 00:00:47,107
(Penny:)Okay. Sheldon,
let me ask you a question.

17
00:00:47,111 --> 00:00:49,281
(Leonard:)Mmm.
If I was
at a train station

18
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,880
(Penny:)and one train could take me
to my current job

19
00:00:51,882 --> 00:00:54,882
(Penny:)and the other train could take
me to an audition for a movie,

20
00:00:54,885 --> 00:00:59,025
(Penny:)which train should I get on?

